SUMMARY:Mandabi (1968)
DTSTART:20260203T023000Z
DTEND:20260203T042000Z
DTSTAMP:20260203T023000Z
UID:Lpdm3yX6FG
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 91 mins (1h31m)\n\nSIFF Movie Club In a new 4K resto
 ration\, Ousmane Sembène’s simple story of a man wrestling with a money
  order emerges as a magnificent parable.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-
 and-events/siff-movie-club/mandabi\n\nEstimated start: 18:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mean Streets (1973)
DTSTART:20260226T033000Z
DTEND:20260226T054000Z
DTSTAMP:20260226T033000Z
UID:in1G3CkEeC
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 112 mins (1h52m)\n\nMartin Scorsese: Maestro of Cine
 ma Feel a dazzling rush of cinematic vitality and dark humor as a young ma
 n (Harvey Keitel)\, split between the rough world around him and his spiri
 tual nature\, tries to keep his loose cannon friend (Robert De Niro) and h
 is girlfriend (Amy Robinson) safe from street toughs and Mob bosses. Inspi
 red by Scorsese’s Little Italy background.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/progr
 ams-and-events/martin-scorsese/mean-streets\n\nEstimated start: 19:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SLC Punk (1998)
DTSTART:20260303T023000Z
DTEND:20260303T042500Z
DTSTAMP:20260303T023000Z
UID:FJyS0Y1ua9
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 97 mins (1h37m)\n\nSIFF Movie Club In this lively co
 medy\, a blue-haired punker and his best pal find their anarchist ideals a
 t odds with life in their starched hometown: Salt Lake City.\n\nhttps://ww
 w.siff.net/programs-and-events/siff-movie-club/slc-punk\n\nEstimated start
 : 18:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Taxi Driver (1976)
DTSTART:20260305T033000Z
DTEND:20260305T054000Z
DTSTAMP:20260305T033000Z
UID:l4bNIDFSpW
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 114 mins (1h54m)\n\nMartin Scorsese: Maestro of Cine
 ma He’s (Robert De Niro) an alienated\, lonely man in an urban snake pit
 \, who sees himself as “an avenging angel” capable of heroic action\, 
 like saving a teen prostitute (Jodie Foster) from her sleazy pimp (Harvey 
 Keitel). People with“bad ideas” in the city of night. 50th anniversar
 y screening.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/martin-scorsese/t
 axi-driver\n\nEstimated start: 19:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Raging Bull (1980)
DTSTART:20260312T023000Z
DTEND:20260312T045500Z
DTSTAMP:20260312T023000Z
UID:J1Iuo5SK1o
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 129 mins (2h09m)\n\nMartin Scorsese: Maestro of Cine
 ma A skilled boxer’s (Robert De Niro) anger serves him well in the ring\
 , but it threatens his relations with his brother (Joe Pesci)\, his new wi
 fe (Cathy Moriarty) and the Mafia\, which wants to control his career. Fig
 ht sequences as poetic ecstasy.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-event
 s/martin-scorsese/raging-bull\n\nEstimated start: 19:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The King of Comedy (1982)
DTSTART:20260319T023000Z
DTEND:20260319T043500Z
DTSTAMP:20260319T023000Z
UID:nkvxlDMMbx
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 109 mins (1h49m)\n\nMartin Scorsese: Maestro of Cine
 ma Mediocre comedian (Robert De Niro) dreams of being on the Comedy King
 ’s (Jerry Lewis) TV show. Maybe his chances would improve if he and his 
 friend (Sandra Bernhard) kidnapped his idol. Delightfully cringey.\n\nhttp
 s://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/martin-scorsese/the-king-of-comedy\n\
 nEstimated start: 19:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:GoodFellas (1990)
DTSTART:20260326T023000Z
DTEND:20260326T051500Z
DTSTAMP:20260326T023000Z
UID:UHlHqgL6pT
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 146 mins (2h26m)\n\nMartin Scorsese: Maestro of Cine
 ma Three mobsters (Ray Liotta\, Robert De Niro\, Joe Pesci) play by Mob ru
 les\, enjoying money\, prestige\, wine women and song “like a rollicking
  road movie.” But they misstep\, triggering a delirious climactic fall f
 rom grace. One of the greatest of all films.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/progr
 ams-and-events/martin-scorsese/goodfellas\n\nEstimated start: 19:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Age of Innocence (1993)
DTSTART:20260402T023000Z
DTEND:20260402T050500Z
DTSTAMP:20260402T023000Z
UID:EawlrVVuKG
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 139 mins (2h19m)\n\nMartin Scorsese: Maestro of Cine
 ma In this adaptation of Edith Wharton’s novel\, 1870s New York society 
 shapes and controls lives. A lawyer (Daniel Day-Lewis) is set to marry a w
 ealthy socialite (Winona Ryder)\, when he falls in love with an outsider (
 Michelle Pfeiffer). Secret love expressed with flowers\, and a glove eroti
 cally removed. Scorsese the romantic.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and
 -events/martin-scorsese/the-age-of-innocence\n\nEstimated start: 19:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cleo From 5 to 7 (1962)
DTSTART:20260407T013000Z
DTEND:20260407T031500Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T013000Z
UID:B8hVdQ4Xa9
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 90 mins (1h30m)\n\nSIFF Movie Club Agnès Varda eloq
 uently captures Paris in the sixties with this real-time portrait of a sin
 ger (Corinne Marchand) set adrift in the city as she awaits test results o
 f a biopsy.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/siff-movie-club/cl
 eo-from-5-to-7\n\nEstimated start: 18:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Casino (1995)
DTSTART:20260409T023000Z
DTEND:20260409T054500Z
DTSTAMP:20260409T023000Z
UID:QM66mHHrNl
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 179 mins (2h59m)\n\nMartin Scorsese: Maestro of Cine
 ma Juicy\, over the top\, deliciously gaudy 1970s excess\, as Robert De Ni
 ro tries to keep his casino free of Mob interference\, while his enforcer 
 (Joe Pesci)\, his wife (Sharon Stone)\, and her ex (James Woods) pursue th
 eir often conflicting agendas. With Don Rickles\, Frankie Avalon\, and Sco
 rsese’s mother Catherine. 30th anniversary screening.\n\nhttps://www.si
 ff.net/programs-and-events/martin-scorsese/casino\n\nEstimated start: 19:4
 5
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
